From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: JohannaWeb <joaocordeiroalmeida@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Treat an element without a primary style as not display:none

stylo#387. An element can reach style invalidation with `ElementData`
allocated but no primary computed style yet: a freshly created node
(blitz `create_element` initialises default `ElementData`) whose ancestor
has an attribute snapshot, so targeted invalidation descends into it
before the normal traversal styles it. `should_process_descendants` calls
`is_display_none`, and `self.primary().unwrap()` aborted the whole
resolve. A not-yet-styled element is not `display: none`, so a missing
primary style answers false and the normal traversal styles it.

Drop when the upstream fix for #387 is released.

diff --git a/data.rs b/data.rs
index ff6120d..e70f83c 100644
--- a/data.rs
+++ b/data.rs
@@ -188,8 +188,19 @@ impl ElementStyles {
     }

     /// Whether this element `display` value is `none`.
+    ///
+    /// Aurora fork (stylo#387): an element can reach style invalidation with
+    /// `ElementData` allocated but no primary computed style yet — e.g. a
+    /// freshly created node (blitz `create_element` initialises default
+    /// `ElementData`) whose ancestor has an attribute snapshot, so targeted
+    /// invalidation descends into it before the normal traversal styles it.
+    /// `should_process_descendants` calls this, and the original
+    /// `self.primary().unwrap()` aborted the whole resolve. A not-yet-styled
+    /// element is not `display: none`, so treat a missing primary as `false`
+    /// and let the normal traversal style it.
     pub fn is_display_none(&self) -> bool {
-        self.primary().get_box().clone_display().is_none()
+        self.get_primary()
+            .map_or(false, |s| s.get_box().clone_display().is_none())
     }

     /// Whether this element uses viewport units.
